// THE ENGINE-SLOTS / ROUTER-CAP SINGLE-AUTHORITY WITNESS (class B3, 2026-11-24).
// One number -- a replica's admitted concurrency -- had two homes: the Strata engine's --parallel
// (written by hand, reserving VRAM per slot) and the router row's cap (derived from the capacity shape).
// srv3 ran slots 8 beside cap 4 (4,642 experts resident, ~6.6 tok/s per conversation); ken ran cap 4
// with the engine unmodeled (1.0 tok/s per stream). The repair makes the JOINED ADMISSION -- the capacity
// shape at the grant of the layout being projected (serving_replica_profile::replica_admission_named) --
// the ONE authority both ends read (engine: replica_engine_launch; router: router_dev_replica_shape), and
// removes the writable slot field from the production launch record. The 2026-11-25 operator review found
// the last split -- the engine reading the profile's grant while the router joined the projected layout --
// and its reduced-grant and refused-grant controls are here. These claims pin BOTH ends to the one
// derivation and carry the 2026-11-24 measurements (with their standing) as the price of the choice. The
// class is filed as
// gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::engine_slots_written_beside_the_admission_that_bounds_them.
module test.claim.serving.replica_engine_admission_witness

